      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SNIPPETY LEGEND (2) boasts the strongest profile despite resuming, and a trial win at Geraldton signals he's ready. He last finished third in a BM70+ here as a well-backed favourite, and with a strong track and trip record, he's the one to beat. GOLD KEEPER (3) is a key danger, having lost to DIVINE INANNA by a neck here last time out. His previous run had merit despite late interference behind Oracle Son. Now third-up with solid form, he can go one better stepping out in distance. DIVINE INANNA (4) deserves respect after defeating GOLD KEEPER while wide on the home turn. Stepping up to this trip is no issue and she maps to get every chance in the run. Can repeat the dose without surprising. PRINCE RAGNAR (1) has been caught after leading in his last two but is race-fit, has a good overall record here, and benefits from a 3kg claim to extend his impact. BAYHARA (6) may be able to dictate from the front and return to winning ways.",
